From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NXForge layer <layer@nxforge.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: upstream-pr-2497: games/0400486024DEC000: a full model heap no longer
 crashes the model rebuild: its CPU buffers and GPU memory are tried again in
 the heap's parents (DM_HEAP_RETRY, on by default)

From seedds/nxnative#2497 (open; 8e6cbe56), taken early for Ocarina of Time. Drop this patch when nxnative lands #2497.

games/0400486024DEC000: a full model heap no longer crashes the model rebuild: its CPU buffers and GPU memory are tried again in the heap's parents (DM_HEAP_RETRY, on by default)

Symptom: Ocarina of Time crashed about 11 minutes in on an iPhone (HookLink's test build): "BufferInitialize: pool has no storage", then h_nvnMemoryPoolGetFlags on a null pool, backtrace main+0x436fb4.

Cause: the game's OptimizeChangeBank thread rebuilds a model's material block (main+0x4366e0) with memory from small per-model heaps and checks none of its four allocations: two CPU buffers from the heap's tryAlloc (lr main+0x436910, +0x436da4) and two blocks of GPU memory from main+0x502050 (lr main+0x436f1c, +0x437098). When the heap is full the game goes on with a null block. Hookshot found the same on PCs (NotRexed/Hookshot issue 1697); its notes give these sites and the sead heap layout (+0x38 the parent).

Fix: patches.py heap_retry, stubs after the game's call: a failure is tried again in the heap's parents (at most 16 for the CPU buffers), the GPU memory last in the game's default heap, then the game goes on where it would have. State page +0x170 / +0x174 count the blocks made elsewhere and the power line logs them when they change; DM_HEAP_RETRY=0 (+0x17c) leaves the game as shipped. v131072 only.

Checked: patch_nso.py on this game's v131072 main patches all four sites (main.changed.tsv) after checking each one's original word; host build; iOS compile check 263 files, 0 failed; test_patches, test_env_switches, test_docs pass. Not run in the game here, and HookLink had not run it on a device when it shipped in 1.8.5.

Ported from HookLink's commit cc6e6b47 (https://github.com/dsi-hub/nxnative/tree/hooklink, MIT); the stubs are theirs. Changes from it: the call sits after dynamic_resolution (main's frame_step has no wide view or half-rate hooks), and a game note.

Co-authored-by: dsi-hub <260802842+dsi-hub@users.noreply.github.com>
